./checks/audits/fed-rate--2026-09-16-unanimous-quarter-point-hike-2026-09-19-since-b75257dd-entailment.log:102:   132	        <p data-layer="narrative">Warsh said persistent inflation falls especially hard on people without financial assets, home equity or retirement-plan equity who live from paycheck to paycheck. For them, the benefit of restoring stable prices is not an investment return but protection of real take-home pay.<Cite s="fomc-press-conference-2026-09-16" passage="people that don't own financial assets" /><Cite s="fomc-press-conference-2026-09-16" passage="they're living off their paycheck" /><Cite s="fomc-press-conference-2026-09-16" passage="deliver real take home pay increases" /></p>
