./checks/audits/fed-rate--2026-09-16-unanimous-quarter-point-hike-2026-09-19-since-b75257dd-entailment.log:150:   180	        <p data-layer="narrative">The dispute was also about what a supply shock calls for. Before the meeting, Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent argued that central banks traditionally do not raise rates after a supply shock unless second- or third-order effects appear, and said core inflation remained restrained.<Cite s="dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31" passage="traditionally you don't raise [rates]...unless you see second or third-order effects" /><Cite s="dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31" passage="core inflation has remained very restrained" /></p>
