   127	## 7. Source and Corroboration Problems
   128	
   129	The 19 listed records do not represent 19 independent confirmations.
   130	
   131	- The statement, implementation note, SEP release, SEP PDF, transcript, video, calendar, and longer-run-goals document are eight Federal Reserve artifacts. They establish different parts of the record but remain one institutional source family.
   132	- The two FRED series and their metadata pages reduce to two underlying data lineages. CSV and metadata copies do not corroborate each other independently.
   133	- The official video and transcript are two renderings of the same press event. Frame-by-frame review found no separate on-screen source beyond the SEP charts.
   134	- The SEP release and full SEP are one projection lineage.
   135	- The PBS record is an Associated Press story, not an independent PBS reporting lineage.
   136	- ABC, CBS, Guardian, The Hill, AP, and CNBC repeatedly confirm the decision, but that fact ultimately originates with the FOMC.
   137	- BLS, BEA, CBO, EIA, and the New York Fed provide genuinely separate primary lineages for the economic and operational context.
   138	- The consumer-effects account has one principal editorial lineage, AP. The political claim originates in Trump’s post and is repeated by several outlets.
   139	
   140	The larger source problem is utilization: the page collected consumer, political, and post-decision interpretation records but left their material content outside the reader-facing account.
